       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication that justifies it, and it carries a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis. A normal creatinine and liver function don't offset that risk.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day).\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specific research context, please talk to pharmacy first. Their sign-off and the hospital's formal override process should come before the order goes in. I'm glad to enter it as soon as one of the options above works for you."
